Package: gitdock
Version: 1.2.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: GitDock Dev <dev@gitdock.dev>
Installed-Size: 5188
Depends: nodejs (>= 18), adduser
Recommends: git (>= 2.30), gh
Suggests: glab, curl, wget
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://gitdock.dev
Description: Local dashboard for managing multiple GitHub (and GitLab) accounts
 GitDock is a web-based utility for managing GitHub and GitLab hosted
 repositories. It provides a local web dashboard that allows users to:
  - list and clone repositories under a defined workspace
  - manage authentication via personal access tokens
  - configure SSH keys per account
  - perform git operations (commit, push, pull, branch, stash)
  - monitor repo activity across multiple machines (via GitDock Hub)
 .
 GitDock runs as a systemd service on localhost:3847 and is accessible
 only from the local machine.
